cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite an RFD, a measurement, a retraction or a constraint from this record, please cite it as below."
title: "request-for-discussion: the reference designs and engineering record for weftspun"
abstract: >-
  The durable decisions behind the weftspun projects, and the engineering
  record that justifies or retracts them. Each Request-for-Discussion is a
  reference design: it records a decision and points at the canonical
  documentation rather than restating it. Beside them sits the logbook, moved
  here when `weftspun/logbook` was archived: what was measured, what it cost,
  and which roads turned out to be dead ends. Entries record the measurement
  rather than the intention and clip the apparatus, so a result can be re-run
  rather than believed. Retractions stay in place next to what they retract,
  because a reader who knows which roads are dead ends is better off than one
  who only knows the current answer.

  Holds the working agreements every project in the workspace is written
  against (CLAUDE.md), the recurring failure modes and the guards that now
  catch them (PITFALLS.md), narrative entries on the soft renderer's
  mis-scaled constants, CineForm in Godot, the edge NPU forward pass and the
  one-repo-per-model reranking, and the gates and apparatus that produced the
  numbers.
